PR Summary & Creation Skill (/pr-summary)
The /pr-summary skill is an automated Pull Request Authoring and Creation Gate. It inspects your current git branch changes, parses the user story acceptance criteria, analyzes the latest Playwright test execution results, synthesizes an executive-grade Pull Request description, and opens the PR via the GitHub MCP Server.

🎯 Standard PR Output Schema
# feat(automation): implement and verify [<STORY_ID>] <Feature Title>

## 📌 1. Feature Overview
- **Work Item / Issue:** [<STORY_ID>](link)
- **Feature Name:** <Feature Title>
- **Target Layer:** UI / REST API / Hybrid E2E
- **Target Branch:** `feature/<story-id>-automation` ➔ `main`

---

## 🎯 2. Acceptance Criteria Coverage (1-to-1 Traceability)
Each acceptance criterion from the user story is verified by a dedicated, isolated test:
- [x] **AC1:** <Criterion 1 description> (`test('AC1: ...')`)
- [x] **AC2:** <Criterion 2 description> (`test('AC2: ...')`)
- [x] **AC3:** <Criterion 3 description> (`test('AC3: ...')`)

---

## 🛠️ 3. Branch Changes
| Component | File Path | Action | Description |
| :--- | :--- | :---: | :--- |
| **Test Spec** | `tests/<feature>.spec.ts` | Added | 1-to-1 AC test scenarios with custom fixtures |
| **Page Object** | `pages/<PageName>.ts` | Updated | Resilient semantic locators and action workflows |
| **API Client** | `services/SpartanApiClient.ts` | Verified | Typed REST endpoints using Playwright APIRequestContext |
| **Test Data** | `test-data/spartanData.ts` | Verified | Strong DTO models and message contracts |

---

## 🧪 4. Playwright Test Execution Results
- **Execution Command:** `npx playwright test <target-spec> --project=chromium`
- **Verdict:** **`PASS ✅`** (100% Tests Passed)
- **Tests Passed:** `<passed>` / `<total>` total
- **Duration:** `<duration>`s
- **HTML Report:** `playwright-report/index.html` (Generated)
- **Failure Screenshots:** 0 (Clean run)

---

## 🛡️ 5. Quality Gate Checklist
- [x] **1. Locator Strategy:** Semantic user-facing locators utilized (`getByRole`, `getByLabel`); zero brittle absolute XPaths.
- [x] **2. Timing & Auto-Wait:** ZERO hardcoded sleeps (`page.waitForTimeout` / `setTimeout`) detected.
- [x] **3. Web-First Assertions:** Retrying `expect(...)` assertions present in every assertion block.
- [x] **4. POM Discipline:** Locators and action workflows encapsulated in `pages/` extending `BasePage.ts`. No assertions in Page Objects.
- [x] **5. Test Isolation:** Dynamic `@faker-js/faker` data utilized for entity inputs to ensure parallel safety.
- [x] **6. Type Safety:** `npm run typecheck` passes with zero TypeScript errors.

---

> 🚀 **Ready for peer review before merging to `main`.**
🤖 GitHub MCP Execution Protocol
Calls GitHub MCP create_pull_request (or Git CLI):
Title: feat(automation): implement and verify [<STORY_ID>] <Feature Title>
Head Branch: Current feature branch (feature/<target-id>-automation)
Base Branch: main
Body: The generated markdown report above.
Returns the URL of the newly created Pull Request in the console.